.TH MD_NEW_WITH_THREADS 3 "2026-10-17" "libmorsedec 0.3.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
md_new_with_threads \- create a decoder with a channel processing thread budget
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <morsedec.h>

morsedec_decoder_t *md_new_with_threads(
    const struct morsedec_config *config, size_t threads);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Construct a mono audio decoder. Input, configuration and ownership match
md_new(3). All storage and workers are created before return.
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I config
Configuration to copy, or NULL for the defaults documented by md_new(3).
.TP
.I threads
Maximum simultaneous processing participants, including the caller. Zero selects
automatic scheduling using online logical CPUs. One creates no workers.
Larger values explicitly enable channel parallelism. Budgets are capped by
max_channels; no CPU affinity or priority is changed.
.SH RETURN VALUE
An owned decoder, or NULL with errno set. md_get_thread_count() reports the
resolved maximum; fewer participants are used when fewer channels have work.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
Invalid decoder configuration.
.TP
.B ENOMEM
Allocation or FFT planning failed, or an explicit worker allocation failed.
.TP
.B ENOTSUP
An explicit threads value greater than one was requested without a thread
backend.
.TP
.B EAGAIN
An explicit request could not create workers because resources were unavailable.
Other pthread initialization errors may also be returned.
.SH REMARKS
Automatic mode runs fewer than four runnable channels serially. Explicit mode
may parallelize two. Each job owns one channel's complete pipeline; FFT, band
management, selection and sorting remain serial. All jobs complete before a
processing call returns. Synchronization may wait for OS scheduling; there is no
additional input queue, allocation, blocking I/O or callback during processing.
.PP
Automatic worker initialization failures clean up partial pools and fall back to
serial. Explicit requests return the failure. Reset retains the pool and budget;
deletion joins workers. Multiple handles have independent pools: choose budgets
that avoid oversubscribing the application. Threading may increase CPU use or
elapsed time for small workloads.
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Serialize construction with every FFTW planner and plan-destruction operation.
Serialize all calls accessing the resulting handle, including queries.
.SH VERSION
Available in the libmorsedec 0.2.0 development API. Version 0.3.0 uses
shared-library ABI 2.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR md_new (3),
.BR md_get_thread_count (3),
.BR md_delete (3),
.BR md_reset (3),
.BR libmorsedec (3)
